<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antium was an ancient town on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latium">Latium</a>, at modern Anzio south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. A Volscian port whose ships raided the coast, it resisted Rome until 338 BCE, when its fleet was taken and the bronze prows (rostra) of its ships were set up on the speakers' platform in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-forum">Roman Forum</a>. Under the empire it was a favoured resort and the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antium.jpg" alt="Antium" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cassius Ahenobarbus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antium_plan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
